A||||7||BN Boomer||Water in trunk
Z||000000||BN Boomer||07-07-99||05:56 PM||||After buying my 87 SE, I noticed that the carpet in the bottom of the trunk was wet. I removed the carpet, cleaned it, and put in the garage to dry out. I thoroughly dried out the trunk as well. After the next rain I noticed the trunk was wet again. The water appears to be entering near what I think are body attaching points on both sides of the trunk. There is also surface rust in this area. Has anybody else had this problem? Any suggestions to remedy it? My initial thought is thoroughly clean the area and apply either a sealant or fiberglass over it.
Z||000001||PaUL||07-07-99||06:33 PM||||Do you have a rear wing? Water could be leaking into the trunk from the 4 holes drilled into the decklid for the wing stantions.
Z||000002||Bruce||07-07-99||07:26 PM||||I have the same problem with my 86 GT, which does have the rear spoiler. What's the best solution?
Z||000003||PaUL||07-07-99||07:34 PM||||To prevent leaks from the rear wing bolt holes, I use a non hardening gasket sealer from Permatex. I think its called Form-a-Gasket or something like that. It comes in a tube and has a consistency similar to tar. I just smear some on the bolts and nuts.
Z||000004||87GT||07-07-99||07:35 PM||||My 87GT also leaks in the trunk, and I too have a wing.  
Z||000005||BN Boomer||07-07-99||08:37 PM||||My SE has the luggage rack and a small wing. I'll check out the mounting screw to see if that's the problem. Thanks for the tip.
Z||000006||DXR_DAD||07-07-99||11:41 PM||||I have an aftermarket tail on my 86, that I put on I filled the hoels in the tail with liquid rubber before installing it. I have done the same on my sons car.<br>It seems to seal when you tighten down the screws.
Z||000007||Guy||07-08-99||07:05 PM||||Good day,<p>I also got water in the trunk of my 87'GT. In removing the carpet, I found two pre-drilled holes directly in the bottom of the trunk. I plugged them with some bolts and silicone and the problem went away. Interestingly enough, my neighbour has an 86'GT and his had the same two holes and problem with water.I am really interested in why these two holes were even there ?<p>Regards,<br>
